{"name":"Cappuccino","hex":"#704a3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cappuccino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian coffee-based beverage made from espresso to which milk that has been steamed or frothed is added.","A cup of this beverage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cappuccino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cappuccino","blocks":[{"text":"Cappuccino is an espresso-based coffee drink traditionally prepared with steamed milk, including a layer of milk foam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Cappuccino_in_original.jpg/330px-Cappuccino_in_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cappuccino","wikidata":"Q159774"},{"title":"Cappuccino (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cappuccino\"  is a single by Japanese entertainer Rie Tomosaka, released on January 27, 1999. \"Cappuccino\" and its B-side \"Mokuren no Cream\" were both written by musician Ringo Sheena. In 2014, Sheena released a cover of the song on her album Gyakuyunyū: Kōwankyoku, which reached number 98 on the Billboard Adult Alternative Chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/RieCappucc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cappuccino_(song)","wikidata":"Q11294647"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg/500px-Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg/1280px-Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg/500px-Bled_%285081159596%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna